<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Augustus III</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Augustus III was Elector of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> and King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and Grand Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> from 1733 to 1763. He owed his election to Russian and Austrian intervention in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-polish-succession">War of the Polish Succession</a>. His largely absent reign was marked by political paralysis in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sejm">Sejm</a>, part of the decline of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/augustus-iii.jpg" alt="Augustus III" width="320" height="411" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Louis de Silvestre · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Louis_de_Silvestre_-_Portrait_of_Augustus_III_of_Poland_(after_1733)_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
